 356:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** * 
 357:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *  This function initializes the BLE Stack, which consists of the BLE Stack 
 358:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *  Manager, BLE Controller, and BLE Host modules. It takes care of initializing
 359:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *  the Profile layer, schedulers, Timer and other platform related
 360:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *  resources required for the BLE component. It also registers the callback 
 361:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *  function for BLE events that will be registered in the BLE stack.
 362:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** * 
 363:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *  Note that this function does not reset the BLE Stack.
 364:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** * 
 365:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *  For HCI-Mode of operation, this function will not initialize the BLE Host 
 366:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *  module.
 367:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** * 
 368:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *  Calling this function results in the generation of CYBLE_EVT_STACK_ON event
 369:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *  on successful initialization of the BLE Stack.
 370:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** * 
 371:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *  \param callbackFunc: Event callback function to receive events from BLE stack.
 372:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *   CYBLE_CALLBACK_T is a function pointer type.
 373:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** * 
