 562:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** ***************************************************************************//**
 563:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** * 
 564:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *  This function writes the new bonding data from RAM to the dedicated Flash 
 565:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *  location as defined by the component. It performs data comparing between RAM
 566:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *  and Flash before writing to Flash. If there is no change between RAM and Flash
 567:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *  data, then no write is performed. It writes only one flash row in one call.
 568:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *  Application should keep calling this function till it return CYBLE_ERROR_OK. 
 569:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *  This function is available only when Bonding requirement is selected in
 570:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *  Security settings.    
 571:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** * 
 572:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *  \param isForceWrite:  If value is set to 0, then stack will check if flash write 
 573:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *                 is permissible. 
 574:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *  
 575:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** * \return
 576:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *  Return value is of type CYBLE_API_RESULT_T.
 577:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *
 578:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *   Errors codes                         | Description
 579:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *   ----------------------------------   | ------------------------------------
 580:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *   CYBLE_ERROR_OK                       | On successful operation
 581:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *   CYBLE_ERROR_FLASH_WRITE_NOT_PERMITED | Flash Write is not complete
 582:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *   CYBLE_ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER        | Invalid input parameter  
 583:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *   CYBLE_ERROR_FLASH_WRITE              | Error in flash Write	
 584:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     
 585:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *  \sideeffect
 586:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *   For BLE devices with 128K of Flash memory this function will automatically 
 587:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *   modify the clock settings for the device.
 588:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *   Writing to flash requires changes to be done to the IMO (set to 48 MHz)
 589:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *   and HFCLK (source set to IMO) settings. The configuration is restored before
 590:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *   returning. This will impact the operation of most of the hardware in the
 591:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *   device.
 592:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** * 
 593:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *  \globalvars
 594:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *   The cyBle_pendingFlashWrite variable is used to detect status
 595:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *   of pending write to flash operation for stack data and CCCD.
 596:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *   This function automatically clears pending bits after write operation 
 597:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** *   complete.
