 748:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     ***************************************************************************//**
 749:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *     
 750:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *  This function is used to start the advertisement using the advertisement data 
 751:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *  set in the component customizer's GUI. After invoking this function, the 
 752:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *  device will be available for connection by the devices configured for GAP 
 753:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *  central role. It is only included if the device is configured for GAP 
 754:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *  Peripheral or GAP Peripheral + Central role.
 755:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *  
 756:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *  On start of advertisement, GAP Peripheral receives the
 757:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *  CYBLE_EVT_GAPP_ADVERTISEMENT_START_STOP event. The following events are 
 758:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *  possible on invoking this function:
 759:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *  
 760:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *  * CYBLE_EVT_GAP_DEVICE_CONNECTED - If the device connects to a GAP Central and 
 761:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *    Link Layer Privacy is disabled in component customizer.
 762:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *  * CYBLE_EVT_GAP_ENHANCE_CONN_COMPLETE - If the device connects to a GAP Central and 
 763:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *    Link Layer Privacy is enabled in component customizer.
 764:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *  * CYBLE_EVT_TIMEOUT: If no device in GAP Central mode connects to this 
 765:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                       device within the specified timeout limit. Stack 
 766:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                       automatically initiate stop advertising when Slow 
 767:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                       advertising was initiated, or starts Slow advertising
 768:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                       after Fast advertising timeout occur.
 769:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *  * CYBLE_EVT_GAPP_ADVERTISEMENT_START_STOP: If device started or stopped
 770:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                                               advertising. Use CyBle_GetState()
 771:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                                               to determine the state. Sequential 
 772:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                                               advertising could be started when
ARM GAS  C:\Users\ARTEM\AppData\Local\Temp\ccm8CtGO.s 			page 15


 773:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                                               CYBLE_STATE_DISCONNECTED state is
 774:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                                               returned.
 775:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     * 
 776:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *  \param advertisingIntervalType: Fast or slow advertising interval with timings
 777:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                                 entered in Advertising settings section of the
 778:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                                 customizer.
 779:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *  * CYBLE_ADVERTISING_FAST   0x00u
 780:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *  * CYBLE_ADVERTISING_SLOW   0x01u
 781:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *  * CYBLE_ADVERTISING_CUSTOM 0x02u
 782:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     * 
 783:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     * \return
 784:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *  CYBLE_API_RESULT_T : Return value indicates if the function succeeded or
 785:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *  failed. Following are the possible error codes.
 786:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     * 
 787:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   Errors codes                      |  Description
 788:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   --------------------------------- |  --------------------------------
 789:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   CYBLE_ERROR_OK                    |  On successful operation.
 790:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   CYBLE_ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER     |  On passing an invalid parameter.
 791:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   CYBLE_ERROR_INVALID_STATE         |  On calling this function not in Disconnected state.
