 913:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     /******************************************************************************
 914:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     * Function Name: CyBle_GapcStartScan
 915:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     ***************************************************************************//**
 916:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     * 
 917:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   This function is used for discovering GAP peripheral devices that are 
 918:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   available for connection. It performs the scanning routine using the 
 919:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   parameters entered in the component's customizer.
 920:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   
 921:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   As soon as the discovery operation starts, CYBLE_EVT_GAPC_SCAN_START_STOP 
 922:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   event is generated. The CYBLE_EVT_GAPC_SCAN_PROGRESS_RESULT event is 
 923:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   generated when a GAP peripheral device is located. There are three discovery
 924:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   procedures can be selected in the customizer's GUI:
 925:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   
 926:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   * Observation procedure: A device performing the observer role receives only
 927:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                            advertisement data from devices irrespective of 
 928:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                            their discoverable mode settings. Advertisement 
 929:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                            data received is provided by the event,      
 930:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                            CYBLE_EVT_GAPC_SCAN_PROGRESS_RESULT. This procedure
 931:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                            requires the scanType sub parameter to be passive
 932:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                            scanning. 
 933:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   
 934:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   * Limited Discovery procedure: A device performing the limited discovery
 935:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                                  procedure receives advertisement data and 
 936:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                                  scan# response data from devices in the 
 937:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                                  limited discoverable mode only. Received data
 938:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                                  is provided by the event, 
 939:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                                  CYBLE_EVT_GAPC_SCAN_PROGRESS_RESULT. This 
 940:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                                  procedure requires the scanType sub-parameter 
 941:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                                  to be active scanning.
 942:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   
 943:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   * General Discovery procedure: A device performing the general discovery 
ARM GAS  C:\Users\ARTEM\AppData\Local\Temp\ccm8CtGO.s 			page 18


 944:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                                  procedure receives the advertisement data and
 945:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                                  scan response data from devices in both 
 946:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                                  limited discoverable mode and the general 
 947:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                                  discoverable mode. Received data is provided
 948:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                                  by the event,
 949:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                                  CYBLE_EVT_GAPC_SCAN_PROGRESS_RESULT. This 
 950:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                                  procedure requires the scanType sub-parameter
 951:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                                  to be active scanning.
 952:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   
 953:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   Every Advertisement / Scan response packet received results in a new event, 
 954:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   CYBLE_EVT_GAPC_SCAN_PROGRESS_RESULT.
 955:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   If 'scanTo' sub-parameter is a non-zero value, then upon commencement of 
 956:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   discovery procedure and elapsed time = 'scanTo', CYBLE_EVT_TIMEOUT event
 957:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   is generated with the event parameter indicating CYBLE_GAP_SCAN_TO.
 958:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   Possible generated events are:
 959:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   * CYBLE_EVT_GAPC_SCAN_START_STOP: If a device started or stopped scanning. 
 960:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                                     Use CyBle_GetState() to determine the 
 961:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                                     state. Sequential scanning could be 
 962:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                                     started when CYBLE_STATE_DISCONNECTED 
 963:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *                                     state is returned. 
 964:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   * CYBLE_EVT_GAPC_SCAN_PROGRESS_RESULT 
 965:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   * CYBLE_EVT_TIMEOUT (CYBLE_GAP_SCAN_TO)
 966:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     * 
 967:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   \param scanningIntervalType:  Fast or slow scanning interval with
 968:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *       timings entered in Scan settings section of the customizer.
 969:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     * 	  * CYBLE_SCANNING_FAST   0x00u
 970:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     * 	  * CYBLE_SCANNING_SLOW   0x01u
 971:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     * 	  * CYBLE_SCANNING_CUSTOM 0x02u
 972:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     * 
 973:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     * \return
 974:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *  CYBLE_API_RESULT_T : Return value indicates if the function succeeded or
 975:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *  failed. Following are the possible error codes.
 976:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *
 977:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   Errors codes                       | Description
 978:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   ---------------------------------- | -----------------------------------
 979:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   CYBLE_ERROR_OK                     | On successful operation.
 980:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   CYBLE_ERROR_STACK_INTERNAL         | An error occurred in the BLE stack.
 981:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *   CYBLE_ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER      | On passing an invalid parameter.
 982:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *  
 983:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     *******************************************************************************/
 984:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     CYBLE_API_RESULT_T CyBle_GapcStartScan(uint8 scanningIntervalType)
 985:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****     {
 986:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c ****         CYBLE_API_RESULT_T apiResult;
 987:Generated_Source\PSoC4/Bluetooth.c **** 
